        "research": {
            "topic": "Errors in AI-generated clinical notes (ambient AI scribes)",
            "summary": "A 2026 JMIR Medical Informatics study of 7,545 AI-scribe clinic notes found 5.3% of evaluated notes contained errors posing serious or imminent risk of harm, with omissions (18%) and hallucinations (11.5%) the most common error types. Roughly 30% of US physicians/practices now use ambient AI scribes, which mostly operate outside FDA oversight and without adverse event reporting.",
