            "description": "AI is now writing clinical notes in about a third of US medical practices, but the largest real-world study found 1 in 20 notes contains an error serious enough to harm patients. Nearly 1 in 5 had important omissions, and over 1 in 10 included hallucinations like medications never taken. With no adverse event reporting system in place, these errors slip into patient records unseen.",
