    "transcript": {
        "duration": 47.81999969482422,
        "text": "1 in 20 AI medical notes carries harmful error. AI clinical notes hide serious errors at 5% of the cases. AI is now writing medical notes in about a third of US practices right now, and the error rate should worry you. In the largest real-world study of AI-generated clinical notes, 1 in 20 contained an error serious enough to cause significant harm to the patient, while in the lens, a nearly 1 in 5 had an important omission, while more than 1 in 10 contained hallucination. Things like medication the patient never took, or symptoms that never made it into the record. The scary part is, these notes read completely fine. The danger is what's missing, not what's written. And because there's no adverse event reporting for these systems, the errors just seep into the patient's records unseen. If you want to study, just comment notes and I'll send it to you.",
        "language": "english",
